  "label": "an add of another message reusing the identity its source holds as a tombstone in the collection is minted beside it, the tombstone left as it stands",
  "note": "imap syncs Archive, which holds basic-1@example.org as a tombstone imap binds under handle 4 with a base, its delete not pushed yet. An add of another message reusing that Message-ID (subject, date and sender differ) does not agree with the row, so it neither revives it nor takes its key: it is keyed by the identity minted over the provisional handle it derives, draws a seq of its own and is staged as a pending create under the provisional handle that key derives. The tombstone keeps its delete. A create under the bare key would rebind it, which the write refuses (SYNC.md section 7; STORAGE.md sections 9 and 10)",
